      "problem": "Which of the following shows the point $D(6,-5)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $D.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $6,$ so we move $6$ units to the *right*, in the positive direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-5,$ so we move $5$ units *down*, in the negative direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/9917f6ae367b802cf686cd847d2ed77641de7e4a0349082c66548f9e461351be.png)",
